//
// The e2e recipes' basedpyright config, driven by the harness-check gate leg
// (latte_harness.check). It is deliberately SEPARATE from harness/pyproject.toml
// rather than a competing ruleset: basedpyright's typeCheckingMode preset only
// re-expands at the top level, so the harness (strict) and the recipes (basic)
// cannot share one run - an executionEnvironment override does NOT re-expand the
// preset. The harness/pyproject.toml [tool.basedpyright] stays the authoritative
// strict config for the package; this file only carries the recipes' delta.
//
// BASIC is a commented ratchet START, not a silent weakening. The recipes read
// raw D-Bus/config JSON that is Any until the recipe model-widening chunk types
// it, so strict drowns them in ~885 unknown-type propagation errors
// (reportUnknownMemberType/VariableType/ArgumentType/LambdaType) that say nothing
// about the recipes' own correctness. Basic drops that family while keeping the
// real checks live (reportArgumentType, missing imports, dead code), so genuine
// bugs are still caught. Strict lands with the model-widening chunk.
{
  "typeCheckingMode": "basic",
  "pythonVersion": "3.14",
  // Resolve the harness package (latte_harness) and its third-party types
  // (pydantic) from the harness's uv-managed venv, identically on and off nix.
  "venvPath": "../../harness",
  "venv": ".venv",
  "include": ["."],
  // The fp4c fixture imports its sibling operation_model via a runtime
  // sys.path.insert basedpyright cannot follow, so put that dir on the path.
  "extraPaths": ["fixtures/fp4c"]
}
